class.description:
One node plays both roles of DIS exercise control. It listens to the Start/Resume, Stop/Freeze, Remove Entity, Create Entity and Acknowledge signals of a [DisNetwork] (found through the group [code]dis_network[/code] unless [member network_path] is set). [b]Managed application.[/b] A Start/Resume or Stop/Freeze PDU addressed to this application (the [member DisNetwork.site_id] and [member DisNetwork.application_id] of the network, where [constant DisSimulationManagementPdu.ID_ALL] matches everything) changes [method get_state] and emits [signal started] or [signal stopped] and [signal state_changed]. If the PDU names a real world time in the future, the change waits for it ([method get_scheduled_time]); a time more than 24 hours ahead is taken as a clock mismatch and applied at once, and a time of 0 means now. A Remove Entity request for one of this application's [DisEntity] nodes emits [signal remove_entity_requested] and, with [member remove_entities], frees the node. A Create Entity request emits [signal create_entity_requested]. With [member auto_acknowledge], every request is answered with an Acknowledge PDU. A request received again within 30 seconds (same originator, PDU type and request ID) is acknowledged again but carried out only once. [b]Simulation manager.[/b] [method send_start_resume], [method send_stop_freeze], [method send_create_entity] and [method send_remove_entity] send a request and return its request ID. A request to one application is sent again every [member retry_interval] until it is acknowledged ([signal acknowledged]) or [member max_retries] resends are used up ([signal request_failed]). A request to all applications is sent once; every answer arrives as [signal acknowledged], and [signal request_failed] is emitted if nobody answered within the time the retries would have taken. [codeblock] @onready var exercise: DisExerciseControl = $DisExerciseControl
func _ready() -> void: exercise.stopped.connect(func(pdu): print("frozen")) exercise.started.connect(func(pdu): print("running, simulation time ", exercise.get_simulation_time()))
func freeze_everyone() -> void: exercise.send_stop_freeze() [/codeblock] Nothing runs in the editor.
